{"author":{"id":"973fc03426eba9a243913e0f6e6823e102397744f60a9ab11c882af948c310c4"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1778942383,"nonce":"sP8evKezZmGPmDFEuV23dMH2LTk=","message":"## Implementation design v0: ledger issue detail and conflict/sync UX\n\nThis issue makes the ledger usable from Mandible's issue and graph surfaces. It should share components between the Issues tab and Graph detail pane instead of building two divergent issue viewers.\n\n### Component boundary\n\nSuggested frontend module layout:\n\n- `ui/src/components/ledger/IssueDetail.tsx`\n- `ui/src/components/ledger/IssueHeader.tsx`\n- `ui/src/components/ledger/IssueBody.tsx`\n- `ui/src/components/ledger/CommentTimeline.tsx`\n- `ui/src/components/ledger/CommentComposer.tsx`\n- `ui/src/components/ledger/RelationshipList.tsx`\n- `ui/src/components/ledger/AuthEvidenceShelf.tsx`\n- `ui/src/components/ledger/SessionHistory.tsx`\n- `ui/src/components/ledger/WorkUnitSummary.tsx`\n- `ui/src/components/ledger/SyncStatusPanel.tsx`\n- `ui/src/components/ledger/ConflictResolutionPanel.tsx`\n\n`IssuesView` and `GraphView` should consume these shared components. Graph compact mode can hide secondary sections by default, but it should not use a separate data model.\n\n### API/data contract\n\nPrefer a canonical detail endpoint once migration provides it, for example:\n\n- `GET /api/ledger/issues/:id`\n- `GET /api/ledger/issues/:id/timeline`\n- `POST /api/ledger/issues/:id/comments`\n- `PATCH /api/ledger/issues/:id`\n- `POST /api/ledger/issues/:id/labels`\n- `POST /api/ledger/conflicts/:id/resolve`\n\nDuring migration, existing `/api/issues/:repoId/:issueId/context` can be mapped into the same frontend detail type. The UI should not care whether the backend is in scanner/shadow/ledger mode as long as the detail type is stable.\n\nRecommended detail type fields:\n\n- `id`: canonical issue ID;\n- `display_id`: short human alias;\n- `project`: display name and project ID;\n- `aliases`: git-bug and other aliases;\n- `title`, `body`, `status`, `resolution`, `kind`, `priority`;\n- `labels` with raw and display names;\n- `author` with actor type/source;\n- `created_at`, `updated_at`, `closed_at`;\n- `comments[]` with actor/source badges;\n- `relationships[]` grouped by type;\n- `work_unit` summary and branch/worktree state;\n- `sessions.active[]`, `sessions.idle[]`, `sessions.historical[]`;\n- `auth_requests[]` / resolution evidence;\n- `sync` status/jobs/outbox summary;\n- `conflicts[]` requiring action;\n- `timeline[]` derived from ledger events when available.\n\n### Issue header UX\n\nHeader should show, compactly:\n\n- title;\n- display ID and project/repo;\n- status and resolution;\n- kind/priority if known;\n- label pills;\n- sync/conflict indicator;\n- primary actions: comment, spawn/resume work, open graph, copy reference.\n\nThe status pill for a closed issue with linked auth request should be actionable: click or keyboard activate should reveal/open the auth evidence shelf. This addresses the earlier concern that auth requests are better represented as evidence/properties of issues in issue mode.\n\n### Body and comments\n\nRender Markdown body and comments safely. Reuse the existing marked + sanitization approach or centralize it into a shared safe Markdown component. Do not duplicate unsafe `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` logic.\n\nComment timeline should show:\n\n- author display;\n- actor type badge: user, agent, system, adapter;\n- source badge: Mandible, git-bug import, auth queue, etc.;\n- timestamp;\n- body;\n- external/source metadata on hover or in an overflow menu.\n\nComment composer:\n\n- writes to ledger command endpoint;\n- optimistic UI is acceptable only if failure rollback is clear;\n- disabled if unresolved sync/conflict policy blocks writes;\n- supports plain Markdown;\n- after submit, clears only when the server confirms success;\n- SSE update should refresh the timeline or insert the created comment.\n\n### Relationships\n\nRelationships should be grouped by type rather than dumped as raw edges:\n\n- Parent/children;\n- Blocks/blocked by;\n- Duplicates;\n- Related/references;\n- Fixed by/caused by;\n- Implements/tests.\n\nEach relationship row should show issue display ID, title, status, and project if needed for disambiguation. Editing relationships can be incremental; display and navigation are required first.\n\n### Auth evidence shelf\n\nIssue detail should show linked auth requests as evidence:\n\n- pending/executing/completed/failed status;\n- title;\n- branch/head branch;\n- approval/result time;\n- linked commits if available;\n- error output tail for failed auth if already captured elsewhere;\n- action to open the Auth tab/request detail.\n\nIn graph compact mode, the shelf can be collapsed behind a count/status chip.\n\n### Sessions and work history\n\nSeparate live state from history:\n\n- active/idle sessions first, with agent type, processing state, branch, and last activity;\n- historical sessions collapsed by default, grouped by agent/provider or date;\n- parent/child sessions represented as nested history if available;\n- action to open/resume session when supported;\n- work unit state/branch/continuation visible without requiring graph navigation.\n\nDo not show dead sessions as if they are currently working.\n\n### Sync and conflict UX\n\nConflict UI must be actionable, not just a warning.\n\nFor each conflict, display:\n\n- field/entity;\n- local value;\n- external value;\n- source adapter/project;\n- when detected;\n- actions: keep Mandible, accept external, manually merge.\n\nManual merge can be simple for first implementation:\n\n- text fields for title/body conflicts;\n- checklist/diff for labels;\n- status selector for status/resolution;\n- relationship picker for relationship conflicts.\n\nSync status should show:\n\n- last imported/exported time;\n- pending outbox count;\n- failed/conflicted count;\n- retry action if backend supports it;\n- adapter lock/retry errors when present.\n\nAvoid making sync UI noisy when everything is clean.\n\n### Layout and scrolling\n\nThe top-level Mandible view should not page-scroll/wiggle. Use fixed-height tab content with intentional internal scroll regions:\n\n- issue list/sidebar scrolls independently;\n- detail body/comment timeline scrolls independently;\n- graph detail pane scrolls internally;\n- composer/action bars remain reachable.\n\nThis is especially important as issue body/comments become longer than current metadata-only detail panes.\n\n### Graph compact mode\n\nGraph detail should use the same `IssueDetail` component in compact mode:\n\n- header always visible;\n- body excerpt/comment count/auth/session/conflict summaries shown first;\n- expandable sections for full body, comments, relationships, sessions, auth evidence;\n- action to open full Issues tab focused on the same canonical issue.\n\n### Tests and verification\n\nRequired tests:\n\n- issue detail renders body/comments safely;\n- actor/source badges render correctly for user/agent/system/imported comments;\n- comment submit calls ledger endpoint, handles success/failure, and updates timeline;\n- conflict panel exposes keep/accept/manual actions;\n- auth evidence shelf opens from closed/status chip;\n- sessions split active/idle/historical correctly;\n- graph compact detail and full issue detail share the same data mapping;\n- no top-level view scroll wiggle at representative desktop/mobile-ish sizes;\n- `npm run build` passes;\n- browser smoke through issue list, issue detail, comment add, graph selection, conflict/sync surface.\n\n### Non-goals\n\n- Do not implement every relationship editing affordance before display/navigation works.\n- Do not build a generic tracker administration UI.\n- Do not require full graph rewrite to show ledger issue detail.\n- Do not hide unresolved conflicts behind a passive icon only.\n\n### Done check\n\nAfter this issue, a user should be able to read an issue's real body/comments, understand who/what changed it, see linked auth/session/work evidence, add comments through the ledger, and resolve sync conflicts without dropping to git-bug or raw DB inspection.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Codex (GPT-5) \u003ccodex@openai.com\u003e","files":null}]}